💡 **SUGGESTION: per-flag "runs when unset" tests duplicate the defaults test**

The three per-flag groups each contain a `runs the X hook when unset (default)` test, and `skipFlagDefaultsTests` additionally asserts all three hooks run together with no flags set — same harness, same setup, same assertion, four times.

The `all three hooks run when no skip flag is set` test at the bottom of the defaults group already proves that the default (`false`) of every flag lets its hook run. Dropping the three per-flag copies (or inverting: fold the combined test into one per-flag assertion) would cut ~30 lines without losing coverage:

```dart
void skipPreJSActionTests() {
  group('CliAgent skipPreJSAction', () {
    test('skips the preJSAction hook when set', () async { ... });
    // 'runs when unset' covered by skipFlagDefaultsTests
  });
}
```

Purely cosmetic — the suite is deterministic and fast either way. Fine to keep as-is if the explicit per-flag symmetry is preferred.

